nL37:     `BOOL SetKernelObjectSecurity(\nL38:       [in] HANDLE               Handle,\nL39:       [in] SECURITY_INFORMATION SecurityInformation,\nL40:       [in] PSECURITY_DESCRIPTOR SecurityDescriptor\nL41:     );\nL42:     `\nL43: ## Parameters\nL44: \nL45: `[in] Handle`\nL46: \nL47: A handle to a kernel object for which security information is set.\nL48: \nL49: `[in] SecurityInformation`\nL50: \nL51: A set of bit flags that indicate the type of security information to set. This parameter can be a combination of the 【8†SECURITY_INFORMATION】 bit flags.\nL52: \nL53: `[in] SecurityDescriptor`\nL54: \nL55: A pointer to a 【9†SECURITY_DESCRIPTOR】 structure that contains the new security information.\nL56: ## Return value\nL57: \nL58: If the function succeeds, the function returns nonzero.\nL59: \nL60: If the function fails, it returns zero. To get extended error information, call 【10†GetLastError】.\nL61: \nL62: ## Requirements\nL63: \nL64: Requirement  | Value\nL65: --- | ---\nL66: Minimum supported client  | Windows XP [desktop apps | UWP apps]\nL67: Minimum supported server  | Windows Server 2003 [desktop apps | UWP apps]\nL68: Target Platform  | Windows\nL69: Header  | securitybaseapi.h (include Windows.h)\nL70: Library  | Advapi32.lib\nL71: DLL  | Advapi32.dll\nL72: ## See also\nL73: \nL74: 【11†GetKernelObjectSecurity】\nL75: \nL76: 【12†Low-level Access Control】\nL77: \nL78: 【13†Low-level Access Control Functions】\nL79: \nL80: 【9†SECURITY_DESCRIPTOR】\nL81: \nL82: 【8†SECURITY_INFORMATION】\nL83: \nL84: 【14†SetFileSecurity】\nL85: \nL86: 【15†SetPrivateObjectSecurity】\nL87: \nL88: 【16†SetUserObjectSecurity】\nL89: \nL90: * * *\nL91: \nL92: ## Feedback\nL93: \nL94: Was this page helpful?\nL95: \nL96: Yes No No\nL97: \nL98: Need help with this topic?\nL99: \nL100: Want to try using Ask Learn to clarify or guide you through this topic?\nL101: \nL102: Ask Learn Ask Learn\nL103: \nL104: Suggest a fix?\nL105: \nL106: * * *\nL107: \nL108: ## Additional resources\nL109: \nL110: *